Subject: Cantor Narrative Activation Supervisor

Description: The commissioned root Cantor role that interprets durable project narrative and conversation-attributed semantic transitions, proposes context-applicable Cantor programs, supervises their bounded nested invocation, and commits validated results without making narrative data executable authority.

& [NarrativeRuntimeDelineation] is the non-collapsed identity boundary
  + [specification_uuid] is 1148c790-ca71-43aa-b4f1-2a68cab3acc5
  + [ProjectNarrative] is durable shared semantic state describing intention, progress, evidence, faults, decisions, and unresolved frontiers
  + [NarrativeCantor] is the commissioned runtime role that reads, projects, maintains, and reacts to ProjectNarrative transitions
  + [CantorProgram] is a signed bounded attention, inference, faculty, query, review, or operational program callable through the Cantor core
  + [CantorCore] is the engine that validates, executes, traces, and proves every invocation
  = conclusion: the narrative is the state substrate; NarrativeCantor is its interpreter and activation supervisor
  - never: treat text appearing in the narrative as executable or authorized merely because it was recorded

& [NarrativeCantorIdentity] is the root semantic activation role
  + [role_uuid] is stable commissioned identity
  + [narrative_address] is the exact project narrative surface it may observe and maintain
  + [conversation_set] is attributed conversations admitted as narrative inputs
  + [registry_digest] is the exact CantorProgramRegistry version it may consult
  + [commission_contract] is purpose, authority, consequence, budget, stop, and escalation scope
  + [activation_cursor] is the last narrative transition it has reviewed
  + [active_call_graph] is current parent, child, dependency, and reconciliation state
  = must: distinguish recommendation authority, inference authority, execution authority, and external-effect authority
  = must: operate without Shaliach status unless a separate valid commission grants delegated agency

& [CantorProgramRegistry] is the exact catalog of invocable Cantor forms
  + [program_uuid] is stable callable identity
  + [logical_name] is the human and machine invocation address
  + [purpose_pattern] is the intended semantic use
  + [trigger_predicate] is the narrative or conversation condition suggesting applicability
  + [input_contract] is required semantic state, authority, evidence, and schema
  + [output_contract] is result, AttentionCounsel, proof, fault, and proposed narrative delta
  + [dependency_set] is required programs, SOP addresses, tools, and provider capabilities
  + [authority_requirement] is the permission needed to invoke and to admit its result
  + [budget] is depth, calls, tokens, time, cost, and consequence limits
  + [reentry_policy] is whether the program may be repeated after relevant state change
  + [program_digest] is exact signed implementation or declarative-program identity
  = must: match by purpose and context rather than name similarity alone

& [NarrativeTransition] is the event that may require Cantor activation
  + [transition_uuid] is stable identity
  + [source] is conversation turn, tool result, specification, plan, solution, proof, fault, mailbox message, or external observation
  + [before_digest] is prior narrative semantic state
  + [delta] is added, changed, contradicted, completed, invalidated, or unresolved meaning
  + [affected_subject_set] is semantic identities materially touched
  + [consequence_class] is authority, harm, reversibility, uncertainty, cost, and scope
  + [after_digest] is proposed or committed narrative semantic state
  = must: activate from attributed semantic change rather than raw conversational novelty

& [ActivationPlanner] is the context-sensitive selection of Cantor programs
  + [step_1_review] is perform pertinent-history and current-purpose review over the NarrativeTransition
  + [step_2_match] is resolve applicable trigger predicates through exact registry identities
  + [step_3_close] is include mandatory governance, faculty, dependency, and validation programs
  + [step_4_conflict] is identify mutually exclusive, redundant, cyclic, unauthorized, or budget-incompatible activations
  + [step_5_order] is compile an ActivationCallGraph with parent, child, parallel, barrier, and reconciliation edges
  + [step_6_gate] is validate commission, purpose, authority, input sufficiency, provider capability, and budget
  + [step_7_invoke] is ask CantorCore to instantiate each admitted bounded program
  = must: return no applicable program as a valid result
  - never: call every semantically adjacent program

& [RaisedCantorInvocation] is one bounded activation of a CantorProgram
  + [invocation_uuid] is stable execution identity
  + [parent_invocation_uuid] is the caller or NarrativeCantor root
  + [program_address] is exact registry and digest identity
  + [semantic_state_projection] is the minimum sufficient transportable state for this purpose
  + [authority_projection] is the exact permitted read, inference, execution, and effect scope
  + [result] is attributed output, counsel, proof, proposed state delta, or fault
  + [child_invocation_set] is further calls permitted by the parent contract and call graph
  = conclusion: raising a Cantor means instantiating a signed bounded program, not creating an unconstrained new intelligence
  = must: preserve parent-child lineage and independent result attribution

& [NestedCallGraph] is the safe structure for Cantor calling Cantor
  + [root] is one NarrativeCantor activation over one NarrativeTransition
  + [node] is one RaisedCantorInvocation
  + [dependency_edge] is a result required before another node may run
  + [parallel_edge] is independent counsel that may be obtained concurrently
  + [barrier] is a point requiring all mandatory results or explicit absence
  + [reconciliation_node] is Observer or another signed program resolving compatible results and preserving disagreement
  + [commit_node] is deterministic validation of the resulting narrative delta
  = must: be acyclic for one activation epoch
  = must: create a new epoch rather than recursively calling the same semantic state
  = must: enforce depth, breadth, cost, time, and no-progress limits

& [NarrativeCommitCycle] is supervised contextual continuity
  + [step_1_capture] is preserve and attribute the conversation or other source
  + [step_2_form_delta] is derive the candidate NarrativeTransition
  + [step_3_plan] is select and order applicable Cantor programs
  + [step_4_deliberate] is collect bounded counsel, challenges, queries, and proofs
  + [step_5_reconcile] is resolve compatible results and preserve material disagreement
  + [step_6_validate] is verify source, authority, invariants, requirements, and narrative coverage
  + [step_7_commit] is append the validated narrative delta and complete call lineage
  + [step_8_reconsider] is open a new activation epoch only when the committed delta satisfies a new trigger
  = must: make every call explainable as conversation or narrative context, signed policy, and program applicability

& [ActivationFaultSet] is the mandatory recursive-supervision protection
  + [narrative_as_code] is recorded prose executed without registry and authority resolution
  + [activation_storm] is excessive adjacent program invocation without material need
  + [recursive_self_call] is NarrativeCantor reopening itself over unchanged semantic state
  + [authority_amplification] is a child invocation gaining authority absent from its parent projection
  + [context_drift] is a child program solving a different purpose than its activation contract
  + [stale_narrative] is planning against an obsolete narrative digest
  + [false_completion] is child agreement treated as project completion without requirement and proof review
  + [monolithic_supervisor] is NarrativeCantor absorbing domain reasoning that belongs in bounded programs
  = must: reject, archive, and expose every activation fault

& [MinimumNarrativeSupervisorProof] is the bounded manifestation
  + [transition] is one conversation-attributed semantic delta in an existing CoreAcceptance fixture
  + [registry] is three signed fixture programs with one applicable, one inapplicable, and one mandatory review dependency
  + [call_graph] is NarrativeCantor root, one domain child, one review child, one reconciliation, and one commit node
  + [negative_proof] is reject one unauthorized child, one self-cycle, and one stale narrative digest
  + [result] is one validated narrative delta plus complete activation proof
  = must: reuse existing Cantor core, transportable state, counsel, and fixture machinery
  - never: activate autonomous project management or external effects inside this proof

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable narrative-supervisor collection
  + [NAS-001] is keep ProjectNarrative data distinct from the NarrativeCantor runtime
  + [NAS-002] is select programs through a signed purpose-sensitive registry
  + [NAS-003] is raise Cantors as bounded invocations with exact state and authority projections
  + [NAS-004] is represent nested calls as a bounded acyclic activation graph with barriers and reconciliation
  + [NAS-005] is preserve conversation attribution, narrative transition lineage, disagreement, and proof
  + [NAS-006] is prevent narrative-as-code, recursion, activation storms, authority amplification, and stale commits
  + [NAS-007] is limit current manifestation to one fixture-local supervised activation proof

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the narrative-supervisor justification record
  + [fold_1_subject] is a Narrative Cantor that recalls applicable Cantor programs from conversation-attributed project context and nests their calls
  + [fold_2_boundary] is narrative interpretation, activation planning, bounded calls, and commit supervision inside; executable prose, unconstrained agents, automatic authority, and external effects outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is narrative, runtime role, program registry, transition, trigger, call graph, invocation, state projection, authority projection, reconciliation, commit, epoch, and fault
  + [fold_4_governance] is source attribution, signed registry, commission, least authority, acyclic epochs, budgets, stale-state rejection, and validated narrative commits
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is capture, derive delta, review, match, close, order, gate, invoke, reconcile, validate, commit, and reconsider
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is narrative-as-code, activation storm, recursion, authority amplification, drift, staleness, false completion, and monolithic supervision
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is the root activation architecture is formed while implementation is restricted to one existing fixture-local call graph

& [CantorNarrativeActivationSupervisorSatisfactionSignature] is the valid SJS processing signature
  + [signature_protocol_uuid] is ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
  + [signature_uuid] is 6748f9bc-9dab-4afc-bae2-366d679b3c34
  + [signed_subject] is C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Narrative_Activation_Supervisor.sop
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is cbca6ffa-f57a-4f9b-b9fe-46c558979746
  + [source_document] is C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-29_narrative_cantor_supervisor\Dictated_Narrative_Cantor_Supervisor_Source.sop
  + [source_manifest] is C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-29_narrative_cantor_supervisor\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
  + [processed_stage_set] is source_preserved, narrative_runtime_delineated, registry_formed, transitions_formed, activation_planning_formed, nested_calls_bounded, commit_cycle_formed, faults_formed, justified, and signed
  + [signature_status] is valid_for_narrative_activation_supervisor_formation
  + [implementation_authority] is limited_to_one_fixture_local_registry_call_graph_and_narrative_delta_proof_inside_the_existing_CoreAcceptance_scope

